    "description": "<p><span class=\"fontstyle0\">The Bottlecap mine is crudely put together, yet a formidable explosive. Bottlecap mines are constructed from a simple container such as a lunchbox, filled with bottle caps and a crude explosive mixture, and </span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">fitted with a sensor and a detonator. The explosive force hurls the caps over a wide area at such speed that they are essentially shrapnel.</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\"><strong>Special:</strong>&nbsp;</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">when constructing a Bottlecap mine, you may add extra bottlecaps; every 10 caps added increases the damage by +1 @fos[DC]</span><span class=\"fontstyle0\">. When the mine detonates, roll the damage rating a second time: the total rolled is the number of intact caps found in the zone where the mine detonated.</span></p>\n<section data-f2d20-recipe=\"core\"><h3>Crafting recipe</h3><dl><dt>Station</dt><dd>@UUID[Compendium.fallout2d20-compendium.en-crafting-stations.Item.CrftChemBench001]{Chemistry Station}</dd><dt>Complexity</dt><dd>5</dd><dt>Skill</dt><dd>@UUID[Compendium.fallout2d20-compendium.en-skills.Item.ejKiqeUyjkahCjQf]{Explosives}</dd><dt>Perks</dt><dd>@UUID[Compendium.fallout2d20-compendium.en-perks.Item.ureiid51WVHnCcSG]{Demolition Expert}</dd><dt>Rarity</dt><dd>Uncommon</dd></dl><h4>Materials</h4><ul><li>Common Materials ×4</li><li>Uncommon Materials ×1</li></ul></section>",
